story_text.value:
I'm a 52-year-old shift worker at a chemical plant in Finland. Four kids, no coding background. Last Christmas I wanted to send a package to my girlfriend's parents in the Philippines and nobody — not the post office, not DHL, not anyone — could give me a straight answer on price or how to do it. Everyone just said &quot;it's probably expensive.&quot;
That frustrated me enough to spend my days off building something that answers that question. I used Gemini to write all the code. I copy-pasted. This took about a month.
This is what came out: <a href="https://github.com/zemloai-ctrl/zemloai-api" rel="nofollow">https://github.com/zemloai-ctrl/zemloai-api</a>

